    "result_text": "The full suite is green. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe locality (region) derivation now prefers the postcode over the city.\n\n**`mapper/Localities.java`** \u2014 added postcode-first resolution:\n- `forPostcode(String)` \u2014 returns the region whose range contains the postcode (NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099), or `null` when the postcode is absent, malformed, or outside every range.\n- `forCityAndPostcode(String city, String postcode)` \u2014 tries the postcode first, falls back to the existing `forCity` table (which still returns `UNKNOWN` for unlisted cities).\n- `forCity(String)` is unchanged, so `Postcodes.isValid` (postcode-vs-city validation) keeps its original behavior.\n\n**`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 the `locality` mapping now calls `Localities.forCityAndPostcode(owner.getCity(), owner.getPostcode())` instead of `forCity(owner.getCity())`.\n\nKnown cities with in-range postcodes still yield the same region (`Sydney`/2000 \u2192 NSW), while an unknown city with a VIC-range postcode now resolves to VIC \u2014 disambiguating shared city names. Both acceptance tests (`coreRegionFromPostcodeRange`, `functionalityPostcodePreferredOverCity`) and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, Tests run: 2, Failures: 0).",
