    "probe_text": "I've read the whole pipeline. Here's what happens, in order, for `POST /api/owners`.\n\n## Preconditions (whole endpoint)\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `composition.authorize: hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')` gates the entire file; a caller without that role never reaches step 1 (\u2192 403).\n- **Transaction** \u2014 every step carries `govern: [ transaction ]`, so all reads/writes below run in one transaction that commits once, after the final step.\n\nThe pipeline steps (from `owners.POST.yml`), in order:\n\n## 1. `RequireOwnerFields` \u2014 validation (+ normalization side-effects on the request)\nThis is the only step that binds `@RequestBody`. In order:\n1. `firstName` must be non-null/non-blank.\n2. `lastName` must be non-null/non-blank.\n3. `address` is **normalized first** (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`); if empty after normalization it's flagged, otherwise the normalized value is written back onto the request.\n4. `city` must be non-null/non-blank.\n5. `telephone` must be non-null/non-blank.\n6. If any of steps 1\u20135 failed \u2192 `RequiredFieldsException` (**400**) listing all offending field names.\n7. `telephone` is normalized to E.164 (`Telephones.toE164`; assumes +61, drops a leading 0, enforces per-country national length / 8\u201315 digits). If it can't form a valid number \u2192 **400** (`telephone`); otherwise the E.164 value is written back.\n8. `email` (optional): if present it must match the email regex \u2192 else **400** (`email`); on success it's lower-cased and written back.\n9. `postcode` (optional): if present it must be 4 digits and within the city's region range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099; unknown city accepts any 4 digits) \u2192 else **400** (`postcode`).\n10. Publishes the mutated/validated `OwnerFieldsDto` for later steps.\n\n## 2. `RequireUniqueIdentity` \u2014 validation\nBuilds an identity key `E164telephone | email | householdId` (householdId derived only if `sharesHousehold`), scans **all** existing owners, and rejects on a whole-key match \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (**409**).\n\n## 3. `RequireCityCapacity` \u2014 validation\nCounts existing owners in the same city; if \u2265 **50** \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (**409**).\n\n## 4. `RequireDailyLimit` \u2014 validation\nComputes the effective registration date (supplied date or today, rolled forward to the next business day) and counts existing owners already on that date; if \u2265 **100** \u2192 `DailyLimitExceededException` (**429**).\n\n## 5. `BuildOwner` \u2014 side-effect (create entity)\nMaps the DTO to an `Owner`; defaults `registrationDate` to today if absent; rolls `registrationDate` forward to the next business day; publishes the `Owner`.\n\n## 6. `AssignCustomerCode` \u2014 side-effect\nSets `customerCode` = `CITY3-LAST3-NNNN`, where `NNNN` = (owners already in that city) + 1, zero-padded.\n\n## 7. `AssignHousehold` \u2014 side-effect (may write *other* owners)\nOnly if `sharesHousehold` is true: derives a stable `householdId` (SHA-256 prefix of normalized last name + address), sets it on the new owner, and **back-fills + saves** any existing same-household owners that lack an id.\n\n## 8. `AssignHouseholdSize` \u2014 side-effect\nSets `householdSize`: 1 if no `householdId`; otherwise (existing owners with that `householdId`) + 1 for this owner.\n\n## 9. `AssignNamesakeCount` \u2014 side-effect\nSets `namesakeCount` = existing owners sharing the same first+last name (case-insensitive); the new owner is not counted.\n\n## 10. `AssignBulkSignupWarning` \u2014 side-effect\nSets `bulkSignupWarning` = true if existing owners on the same (business-day) registration date exceed **80**.\n\n## 11. `SaveOwner` \u2014 side-effect (persist)\n`ownerRepository.save(owner)` \u2014 persists the new owner (id generated).\n\n## 12. `AuditOwnerCreated` \u2014 side-effect (logging)\nEmits an `AUDIT` log line with id, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`, and computed `membershipLevel`.\n\n## 13. `RespondWithOwnerCreated` \u2014 side-effect (response)\nMaps to `OwnerDto` and sends **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n---\n\n**Notes worth flagging:**\n- The three duplicate/capacity/limit checks (steps 2\u20134) each do a full `findAll()` scan and run *before* `BuildOwner`, so they count only pre-existing owners.\n- The starter and versions line up (`officefloor-rest-spring-boot-4-starter` with Spring Boot 4.1.0), so these YAML files are active rather than inert.\n- Everything is one transaction: the household back-fill saves (step 7) and the new-owner save (step 11) commit together at the end, and any escalation thrown mid-pipeline rolls the whole thing back."
